    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Stencil processor for finitive volume calculations within CVFEM scheme (Weis et al., Geofluids, 2014).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Philipp Weis, ETH Zuerich </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1contact">
<title>Contact</title><para><ulink url="mailto:philipp.weis@erdw.ethz.ch">philipp.weis@erdw.ethz.ch</ulink></para>
<para>@changes changes Latest Changes</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1motivation">
<title>Motivation</title><para>Specialized stencil processor for PHX scheme.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1usage">
<title>Usage</title><para>To be used within the CVFEM scheme (Weis et al., Geofluids, 2014).</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">Performs<sp/>finite<sp/>volume<sp/>fluxes<sp/>across<sp/>facets.</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1dependencies">
<title>Dependencies</title><para>The functions are tailored for use in <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_explicit_finite_volume_transport_p_h_x" kindref="compound">ExplicitFiniteVolumeTransportPHX</ref></para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1issues">
<title>Known issues</title></sect1>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1testing">
<title>Testing</title><para>testing was done in the period before publication in 2014. </para>
</sect1>
